<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Cispadane Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1796 CE – 1797 CE · capital Bologna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived French-backed republic south of the Po whose congress adopted the green, white and red tricolour, ancestor of the Italian flag.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1796 French victories ended Este rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> and papal rule in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-bologna">Bologna</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a>. Delegates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a>, Ferrara, Modena and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reggio-emilia">Reggio</a> met in congress at Reggio and Modena, and in December 1796 proclaimed the Cispadane Republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>On 7 January 1797 the congress at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reggio-emilia">Reggio</a> adopted the green, white and red tricolour as its flag, now celebrated as the birth of the Italian flag. The republic drafted a constitution modelled on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-first-republic">French Directory</a> and held elections in early 1797. It depended entirely on French protection, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-bologna">Bologna</a> was its main centre.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Only months later, in July 1797, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> merged the Cispadane Republic with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/transpadane-republic">Transpadane Republic</a> to create the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cisalpine-republic">Cisalpine Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cispadane-republic.jpg" alt="Cispadane Republic" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: work · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Cispadane_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1796 CE – 1797 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bologna</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, Emilian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Repubblica Cispadana</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1796&amp;focus=cispadane-republic" aria-label="Cispadane Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4951 604 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cispadane Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5271 860L5261 855M5271 860L5271 860M5271 860L5054 728M5271 860L5218 830"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5261 855h0M5271 860h0M5054 728h0M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5271 860h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5271 860h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1796&amp;focus=cispadane-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
